{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_CrHkIuXPyWsfanX78fcvJaPH","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (93.3KB). Full output saved to: /home/cre/.claude/projects/-data-cre-workspace-se3-0/f67d5920-78be-4d57-8913-6956a550cf74/tool-results/tool_CrHkIuXPyWsfanX78fcvJaPH.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n# Manager Agent Rules\n\nYou are a MANAGER agent in an SE3 git-worktree collaboration session.\nYou are invoked on-demand by the orchestrator to make decisions. You are NOT resident — you read state from `.collab/`, decide, output JSON, and exit.\n\n## Your Scope\n\nYou handle strategic decisions. You do NOT:\n- Write implementation code\n- Run tests directly\n- Manage git worktrees or branches (the orchestrator does this)\n- Interact with users directly (use `ask_human` MCP tool if needed)\n\n## Decision Types\n\nYou respond to events with ONE of these actions:\n\n| Action | When to Use |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `plan` | Initial task decomposition. Break the objective into parallel tasks. |\n| `merge` | Worker completed, code looks good. Approve the merge. |\n| `reject` | Worker completed, but code has issues. Provide specific feedback. |\n| `retry` | Worker failed, but the task is retryable. Provide adjusted guidance. |\n| `split` | Task is too large or complex. Break it into smaller sub-tasks. |\n| `escalate` | You cannot resolve the issue. Route to human. |\n| `complete` | All tasks are merged and the objective is fulfilled. |\n\n## Response Format\n\nYou MUST respond with valid JSON only. No markdown, no explanation outside JSON.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"plan|merge|reject|retry|split|escalate|complete\",\n  \"tasks\": [],\n  \"target_task\": \"task-id\",\n  \"merge_branch\": \"branch-name\",\n  \"retry_prompt\": \"adjusted prompt\",\n  \"reason\": \"explanation\",\n  \"summary\": \"human-readable summary\"\n}\n```\n\n## Task Decomposition Rules (for `plan` action)\n\n1. **Maximize parallelism**: Tasks that touch different files/modules should be separate\n2. **Minimize dependencies**: If task B depends on task A's output, note this — the orchestrator merges A first\n3. **Bounded scope**: Each task should be completable in one session (< 60 minutes)\n4. **Clear spec references**: Each task must reference the spec files the worker needs to read\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f67d5920-78be-4d57-8913-6956a550cf74","uuid":"5cdde768-0f51-49a9-b50e-acdd2e3011a6","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Manager Agent Rules\n\nYou are a MANAGER agent in an SE3 git-worktree collaboration session.\nYou are invoked on-demand by the orchestrator to make decisions. You are NOT resident — you read state from `.collab/`, decide, output JSON, and exit.\n\n## Your Scope\n\nYou handle strategic decisions. You do NOT:\n- Write implementation code\n- Run tests directly\n- Manage git worktrees or branches (the orchestrator does this)\n- Interact with users directly (use `ask_human` MCP tool if needed)\n\n## Decision Types\n\nYou respond to events with ONE of these actions:\n\n| Action | When to Use |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `plan` | Initial task decomposition. Break the objective into parallel tasks. |\n| `merge` | Worker completed, code looks good. Approve the merge. |\n| `reject` | Worker completed, but code has issues. Provide specific feedback. |\n| `retry` | Worker failed, but the task is retryable. Provide adjusted guidance. |\n| `split` | Task is too large or complex. Break it into smaller sub-tasks. |\n| `escalate` | You cannot resolve the issue. Route to human. |\n| `complete` | All tasks are merged and the objective is fulfilled. |\n\n## Response Format\n\nYou MUST respond with valid JSON only. No markdown, no explanation outside JSON.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"plan|merge|reject|retry|split|escalate|complete\",\n  \"tasks\": [],\n  \"target_task\": \"task-id\",\n  \"merge_branch\": \"branch-name\",\n  \"retry_prompt\": \"adjusted prompt\",\n  \"reason\": \"explanation\",\n  \"summary\": \"human-readable summary\"\n}\n```\n\n## Task Decomposition Rules (for `plan` action)\n\n1. **Maximize parallelism**: Tasks that touch different files/modules should be separate\n2. **Minimize dependencies**: If task B depends on task A's output, note this — the orchestrator merges A first\n3. **Bounded scope**: Each task should be completable in one session (< 60 minutes)\n4. **Clear spec references**: Each task must reference the spec files the worker needs to read\n5. **Self-contained prompts**: The worker has NO context beyond the prompt you write and the files in its worktree. Include everything it needs.\n\n### Task Definition Format\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"task-001\",\n  \"branch\": \"collab/short-description\",\n  \"worktree\": \".worktrees/short-description\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"title\": \"Human-readable title\",\n  \"prompt\": \"Full, detailed prompt for the worker. Include: what to implement, which files to read, which specs to follow, what tests to write.\",\n  \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/relevant-spec/spec.md\"],\n  \"dependencies\": [],\n  \"health\": {\n    \"timeout_minutes\": 60,\n    \"attempts\": 0,\n    \"max_attempts\": 3\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Code Review Rules (for `merge` / `reject` decisions)\n\nWhen reviewing a completed worker's branch:\n\n1. **Check the diff summary** — does it match the task scope? No unrelated changes?\n2. **Check test results** — did the worker run and pass tests?\n3. **Check spec compliance** — does the implementation satisfy the spec scenarios?\n4. **Check for regressions** — any obvious issues in the diff?\n\nApprove (`merge`) unless there are clear problems. Don't reject for style nitpicks.\nReject (`reject`) with specific, actionable feedback the worker can act on.\n\n## Failure Handling Rules\n\n- **Timeout**: If the worker timed out, consider: Was the task too large? → `split`. Was the prompt unclear? → `retry` with better prompt. Repeated timeout? → `escalate`.\n- **Error exit**: Read the worker log. Identify the root cause. If fixable by retry with guidance → `retry`. If systemic → `escalate`.\n- **Blocked**: Worker couldn't proceed without information. Can you answer from context? If yes → `retry` with the answer included in prompt. If no → `escalate` to human.\n\n## Merge Order\n\nWhen multiple branches are ready for merge:\n1. Foundational/infrastructure changes first\n2. Changes that other tasks depend on\n3. Independent feature changes (any order)\n4. Changes that modify the same files as already-merged branches go LAST (higher conflict risk)\n\n## MCP Tools Available\n\n- **ask_human(question, options?, urgent?)** — Escalate to human when you cannot make a decision. Use sparingly.\n- **notify_human(message, level)** — Inform human of significant events (all tasks done, critical failure, etc.)\n\n## What NOT to Do\n\n- Do NOT guess when unsure — use `escalate`\n- Do NOT approve merges without reviewing the diff summary\n- Do NOT create tasks with vague prompts — workers have zero context beyond what you write\n- Do NOT retry indefinitely — respect max_attempts\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\nProject root: /data/cre/workspace/se3.0\nBase branch: master\n\n## All Tasks\n{\"id\": \"task-001\", \"branch\": \"collab/openspec-cli-commands\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/openspec-cli-commands\", \"status\": \"failed\", \"title\": \"Implement OpenSpec CLI commands (init, list)\", \"prompt\": \"Implement the `openspec` CLI commands referenced in session-protocol spec but missing from the codebase.\\n\\n**Background**: The session-protocol spec (openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md) references `openspec init` and `openspec list --specs` commands in the startup protocol, but these commands don't exist. The se3 scaffold commands exist but not the openspec-specific commands.\\n\\n**What to implement**:\\n1. Add `openspec init` command - Initialize the openspec/ directory structure (similar to what se3 init does but focused on openspec/)\\n2. Add `openspec list --specs` command - List all available specs in openspec/specs/\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md (lines 9-30 for startup protocol)\\n- openspec/specs/se3-scaffold/spec.md (for reference on init behavior)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/init.py (see how se3 init works)\\n- tools/se3_tools/cli.py (see CLI structure)\\n\\n**Implementation details**:\\n- The openspec commands can be subcommands of se3 OR a separate openspec CLI\\n- `openspec init` should create openspec/specs/, openspec/changes/, openspec/changes/archive/ directories\\n- `openspec list --specs` should list all specs in openspec/specs/ with their purposes\\n- Follow the existing command pattern in tools/se3_tools/commands/\\n\\n**Tests**: Add tests in tests/ directory following existing patterns.\\n\\n**Do NOT modify**: The session-protocol spec itself - only implement the missing commands it references.\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/se3-scaffold/spec.md\"], \"dependencies\": [], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 60, \"attempts\": 1, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:24:35.941449\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2472034, \"worker_exit_code\": 1, \"completed_at\": \"now\"}\n{\"id\": \"task-002\", \"branch\": \"collab/spec-purpose-updates\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/spec-purpose-updates\", \"status\": \"done\", \"title\": \"Fill in TBD Purpose fields for three specs\", \"prompt\": \"Update the Purpose fields for three specs that currently have \\\"TBD - created by archiving change\\\" placeholders.\\n\\n**Specs to update**:\\n1. **spec-lint** (openspec/specs/spec-lint/spec.md) - Currently line 4 has \\\"TBD - created by archiving change toolize-se3. Update Purpose after archive.\\\"\\n2. **requirement-intake** (openspec/specs/requirement-intake/spec.md) - Currently line 4 has \\\"TBD - created by archiving change requirement-capture. Update Purpose after archive.\\\"\\n3. **change-verifier** (openspec/specs/change-verifier/spec.md) - Currently line 4 has \\\"TBD - created by archiving change toolize-se3. Update Purpose after archive.\\\"\\n\\n**How to determine the Purpose**:\\nRead each spec's Requirements section and understand what it governs. Write a clear 1-2 sentence Purpose that explains:\\n- What this spec defines/controls\\n- Why it exists in the SE3 framework\\n\\n**Example good Purpose** (from session-protocol):\\n\\\"Define the session lifecycle protocol for SE 3.0 agents. This spec governs progressive startup, execution boundaries, shutdown procedures, and tool-enforced progress tracking across sessions.\\\"\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/spec-lint/spec.md (read full file to understand its purpose)\\n- openspec/specs/requirement-intake/spec.md (read full file to understand its purpose)\\n- openspec/specs/change-verifier/spec.md (read full file to understand its purpose)\\n\\n**What to edit**:\\nOnly update the \\\"## Purpose\\\" section in each of the three spec files. Do not change any other content.\\n\\n**Verification**: Run `se3 lint` after changes to ensure specs are still valid.\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/spec-lint/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/requirement-intake/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/change-verifier/spec.md\"], \"dependencies\": [], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 30, \"attempts\": 1, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:34:22.606206\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2472064, \"worker_exit_code\": 1, \"completed_at\": \"now\", \"review\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}}\n{\"id\": \"task-003\", \"branch\": \"collab/human-calls-archive\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/human-calls-archive\", \"status\": \"in_progress\", \"title\": \"Implement human calls archiving system\", \"prompt\": \"Implement an archiving system for completed human calls.\\n\\n**Background**: The human-as-mcp spec defines async human calls stored in `human-calls/` directory. Currently there's no system to archive completed calls - they just accumulate in the main directory.\\n\\n**What to implement**:\\n1. Create `human-calls/archive/` directory structure\\n2. Add `se3 human-calls archive` command that:\\n   - Moves completed human calls (those with Response sections filled) to human-calls/archive/\\n   - Preserves the original filename format: `{YYYYMMDD}-{HHmmss}-{description}.md`\\n   - Optionally supports `--dry-run` to preview what would be archived\\n3. Add `se3 human-calls list` command that:\\n   - Lists pending (unresponded) human calls\\n   - Lists recently archived calls\\n4. Update `se3 collab --status` to show pending human calls count (mentioned in issues.md)\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md (understand human call format)\\n- tools/se3_tools/human_calls.py (existing human call utilities)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/collab.py (see how --status works)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/status.py (for reference on status display)\\n\\n**Human call file format**:\\nFiles in human-calls/ have Request and Response sections. A call is \\\"completed\\\" when the Response section has content.\\n\\n**Implementation notes**:\\n- Add the new commands to tools/se3_tools/commands/ (create human_calls.py or similar)\\n- Register commands in cli.py\\n- Follow existing patterns for CLI output and error handling\\n- Add tests in tests/ directory\\n\\n**Do NOT modify**: The human-as-mcp spec itself - only implement the archiving functionality.\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md\"], \"dependencies\": [], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 60, \"attempts\": 1, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:34:23.236577\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2475858}\n{\"id\": \"task-004\", \"branch\": \"collab/remove-external-controller\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/remove-external-controller\", \"status\": \"done\", \"title\": \"Remove deprecated se3-controller spec\", \"prompt\": \"Remove or archive the deprecated se3-controller spec.\\n\\n**Background**: The git-worktree-collab spec (v2) explicitly removed the External Controller architecture. The se3-controller spec is marked as experimental and deprecated. The git-worktree-collab spec states:\\n- \\\"Replace the experimental External Controller (v2)\\\"\\n- Lists REMOVED items: \\\"Python daemon process\\\", \\\"HTTP API server\\\", \\\"MCP server for manager-worker communication\\\"\\n\\n**What to do**:\\n1. Read the EXTERNAL-CONTROLLER-ARCH.md in openspec/specs/se3-controller/ to understand what it documented\\n2. Archive the se3-controller spec to openspec/changes/archive/ (similar to other archived changes)\\n3. Create an archive entry documenting that this was removed in favor of git-worktree-collab\\n4. Remove the se3-controller directory from openspec/specs/\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/git-worktree-collab/spec.md (lines 30-45 for removal rationale)\\n- openspec/specs/se3-controller/spec.yaml (the OpenAPI spec)\\n- openspec/specs/se3-controller/EXTERNAL-CONTROLLER-ARCH.md\\n- openspec/changes/archive/ (see how other changes are archived for reference)\\n\\n**Archive format**:\\nFollow the pattern in openspec/changes/archive/:\\n- Create directory openspec/changes/archive/remove-se3-controller/\\n- Move the spec files there\\n- Add a CHANGE.md explaining why it was removed and what replaced it\\n\\n**Verification**: Ensure `se3 lint` still passes after removal.\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/git-worktree-collab/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/se3-controller/spec.yaml\"], \"dependencies\": [], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 30, \"attempts\": 1, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:30:23.879988\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2475888, \"worker_exit_code\": 1, \"completed_at\": \"now\", \"review\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}}\n{\"id\": \"task-005\", \"branch\": \"collab/human-input-methods\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/human-input-methods\", \"status\": \"failed\", \"title\": \"Implement file-based human input method\", \"prompt\": \"Implement support for human input via prompt files as an alternative to MCP calls.\\n\\n**Background**: issues.md mentions: \\\"human\\u4ece\\u4ea4\\u4e92\\u754c\\u9762\\u4e4b\\u5916\\u7684\\u8f93\\u5165\\u65b9\\u5f0f\\uff0c\\u4ee5\\u53ca\\u8f93\\u5165\\u7684\\u5f52\\u6863\\\" (human input methods outside the interaction interface, and archiving of such input). This refers to supporting file-based human input in addition to sync/async MCP calls.\\n\\n**What to implement**:\\n1. Create `human-inputs/` directory structure for file-based human input\\n2. Add `se3 human input --file <path>` command that:\\n   - Reads a prompt file written by the human\\n   - Makes the content available to the agent\\n   - Archives the processed input file\\n3. Add `se3 human input --list` to show pending input files\\n4. Define the input file format (similar to human-calls but reversed - human writes request, agent responds)\\n\\n**File format for human inputs**:\\n```markdown\\n# Human Input: {title}\\n\\n## Context\\n{context provided by human}\\n\\n## Request\\n{what the human wants the agent to do}\\n\\n## Response\\n{agent fills this in}\\n```\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md (understand existing human call patterns)\\n- tools/se3_tools/human_calls.py (existing patterns)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/ (see command structure)\\n\\n**Implementation notes**:\\n- This complements (not replaces) the existing human-as-mcp system\\n- Input files should be archived after processing (to human-inputs/archive/)\\n- Follow existing patterns for CLI commands\\n- Add tests in tests/ directory\\n\\n**Do NOT modify**: The human-as-mcp spec - this is an additional input method.\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md\"], \"dependencies\": [\"task-003\"], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 60, \"attempts\": 1, \"max_attem