{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_5UJSx06a9XGGcm7R078Y7PUf","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (89.5KB). Full output saved to: /home/cre/.claude/projects/-data-cre-workspace-se3-0/f67d5920-78be-4d57-8913-6956a550cf74/tool-results/tool_5UJSx06a9XGGcm7R078Y7PUf.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n---\n\n## Current State\nProject root: /data/cre/workspace/se3.0\nBase branch: master\n\n## All Tasks\n{\"id\": \"task-001\", \"branch\": \"collab/openspec-cli-commands\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/openspec-cli-commands\", \"status\": \"failed\", \"title\": \"Implement OpenSpec CLI commands (init, list)\", \"prompt\": \"Implement the `openspec` CLI commands referenced in session-protocol spec but missing from the codebase.\\n\\n**Background**: The session-protocol spec (openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md) references `openspec init` and `openspec list --specs` commands in the startup protocol, but these commands don't exist. The se3 scaffold commands exist but not the openspec-specific commands.\\n\\n**What to implement**:\\n1. Add `openspec init` command - Initialize the openspec/ directory structure (similar to what se3 init does but focused on openspec/)\\n2. Add `openspec list --specs` command - List all available specs in openspec/specs/\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md (lines 9-30 for startup protocol)\\n- openspec/specs/se3-scaffold/spec.md (for reference on init behavior)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/init.py (see how se3 init works)\\n- tools/se3_tools/cli.py (see CLI structure)\\n\\n**Implementation details**:\\n- The openspec commands can be subcommands of se3 OR a separate openspec CLI\\n- `openspec init` should create openspec/specs/, openspec/changes/, openspec/changes/archive/ directories\\n- `openspec list --specs` should list all specs in openspec/specs/ with their purposes\\n- Follow the existing command pattern in tools/se3_tools/commands/\\n\\n**Tests**: