s - they just accumulate in the main directory.\\n\\n**What to implement**:\\n1. Create `human-calls/archive/` directory structure\\n2. Add `se3 human-calls archive` command that:\\n   - Moves completed human calls (those with Response sections filled) to human-calls/archive/\\n   - Preserves the original filename format: `{YYYYMMDD}-{HHmmss}-{description}.md`\\n   - Optionally supports `--dry-run` to preview what would be archived\\n3. Add `se3 human-calls list` command that:\\n   - Lists pending (unresponded) human calls\\n   - Lists recently archived calls\\n4. Update `se3 collab --status` to show pending human calls count (mentioned in issues.md)\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md (understand human call format)\\n- tools/se3_tools/human_calls.py (existing human call utilities)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/collab.py (see how --status works)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/status.py (for reference on status display)\\n\\n**Human call file format**:\\nFiles in human-calls/ have Request and Response sections. A call is \\\"completed\\\" when the Response section has content.\\n\\n**Implementation notes**:\\n- Add the new commands to tools/se3_tools/commands/ (create human_calls.py or similar)\\n- Register commands in cli.py\\n- Follow existing patterns for CLI output and error handling\\n- Add tests in tests/ directory\\n\\n**Do NOT modify**: The human-as-mcp spec itself - only implement the archiving functionality.\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md\"], \"dependencies\": [], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 60, \"attempts\": 1, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:34:23.236577\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2475858}\n{\"id\": \"task-004\", \"branch\": \"collab/remove-external-controller\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/remove-external-controller\", \"status\": \"done\", \"title\": \"Remove deprecated se3-controller spec\", \"prompt\": \"Remove or archive the deprecated se3-controller spec.\\n\\n**Background**: The git-worktree-collab spec (v2) explicitly removed the External Controller architecture. The se3-controller spec is marked as experimental and deprecated. The git-worktree-collab spec states:\\n- \\\"Replace the experimental External Controller (v2)\\\"\\n- Lists REMOVED items: \\\"Python daemon process\\\", \\\"HTTP API server\\\", \\\"MCP server for manager-worker communication\\\"\\n\\n**What to do**:\\n1. Read the EXTERNAL-CONTROLLER-ARCH.md in openspec/specs/se3-controller/ to understand what it documented\\n2. Archive the se3-controller spec to openspec/changes/archive/ (similar to other archived changes)\\n3. Create an archive entry documenting that this was removed in favor of git-worktree-collab\\n4. Remove the se3-controller directory from openspec/specs/\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/git-worktree-collab/spec.md (lines 30-45 for removal rationale)\\n- openspec/specs/se3-controller/spec.yaml (the OpenAPI spec)\\n- openspec/specs/se3-controller/EXTERNAL-CONTROLLER-ARCH.md\\n- openspec/changes/archive/ (see how other changes are archived for reference)\\n\\n**Archive format**:\\nFollow the pattern in openspec/changes/archive/:\\n- Create directory openspec/changes/archive/remove-se3-controller/\\n- Move the spec files there\\n- Add a CHANGE.md explaining why it was removed and what replaced it\\n\\n**Verification**: Ensure `se3 lint` still passes after removal.\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/git-worktree-collab/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/se3-controller/spec.yaml\"], \"dependencies\": [], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 30, \"attempts\": 1, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:30:23.879988\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2475888, \"worker_exit_code\": 1, \"completed_at\": \"now\", \"review\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}}\n{\"id\": \"task-005\", \"branch\": \"collab/human-input-methods\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/human-input-methods\", \"status\": \"failed\", \"title\": \"Implement file-based human input method\", \"prompt\": \"Implement support for human input via prompt files as an alternative to MCP calls.\\n\\n**Background**: issues.md mentions: \\\"human\\u4ece\\u4ea4\\u4e92\\u754c\\u9762\\u4e4b\\u5916\\u7684\\u8f93\\u5165\\u65b9\\u5f0f\\uff0c\\u4ee5\\u53ca\\u8f93\\u5165\\u7684\\u5f52\\u6863\\\" (human input methods outside the interaction interface, and archiving of such input). This refers to supporting file-based human input in addition to sync/async MCP calls.\\n\\n**What to implement**:\\n1. Create `human-inputs/` directory structure for file-based human input\\n2. Add `se3 human input --file <path>` command that:\\n   - Reads a prompt file written by the human\\n   - Makes the content available to the agent\\n   - Archives the processed input file\\n3. Add `se3 human input --list` to show pending input files\\n4. Define the input file format (similar to human-calls but reversed - human writes request, agent responds)\\n\\n**File format for human inputs**:\\n```markdown\\n# Human Input: {title}\\n\\n## Context\\n{context provided by human}\\n\\n## Request\\n{what the human wants the agent to do}\\n\\n## Response\\n{agent fills this in}\\n```\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md (understand existing human call patterns)\\n- tools/se3_tools/human_calls.py (existing patterns)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/ (see command structure)\\n\\n**Implementation notes**:\\n- This complements (not replaces) the existing human-as-mcp system\\n- Input files should be archived after processing (to human-inputs/archive/)\\n- Follow existing patterns for CLI commands\\n- Add tests in tests/ directory\\n\\n**Do NOT modify**: The human-as-mcp spec - this is an additional input method.\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md\"], \"dependencies\": [\"task-003\"], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 60, \"attempts\": 1, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:34:03.145761\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \